            <div xml:id="d834">

                <pb facs="0886" n="788" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg788"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102H/325: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reinsch</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-06-09T21:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 9, 1919—9
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received June 9—5:45 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Your [<hi rendition="#italic">my</hi>] October 1st, 1917. Decision in this matter
                    is urgent as [activity] of American firm greatly prejudiced by failure to <pb
                        facs="0887" n="789" xml:id="pg789"/> [acquire] land in Harbin. I beg to
                    request authorization to agree to Anglo-Russian agreement with view safeguarding
                    of [interests].</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
